A||||1||mrfixit58||Intermittent Tach
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-27-99||04:03 PM||||Anyone have an idea where to look to repair a tach that sometimes work and other times does not. i've already replaced the tach filter with a Rodney Dickman unit and it didn't make a difference. Once, while I replaced the battery, it started to work again but stopped when I shut the car off and started it again. Does the terminal block next to the battery have anything to do with the tach?
Z||000001||DJRice||07-28-99||09:58 AM||||The terminal block next to the battery has to do with everything electronic connected to the engine.  First, I would check for loose connections at the distributor.  That is where the tach signal originates.  Sometimes the connectors can be on but the wire can be loose in the connector.<p>If that does not do it, start checking all of your ground straps and wires.<p>
